m”, Journal of the ACM 9, 1962; Held and Karp,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“A dynamic programming approach to sequencing problems”, Journal of SIAM 10, 1962): the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none; among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeldKarpTSP"},{"type":"text","text":"’s tour). The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three vertices."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shortestTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/shortestTour(weight:)","role":"symbol","title":"shortestTour(weight:)"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/hamiltonianPath()":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","text":"Path","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()","abstract":[{"text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, extending through each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindHamiltonianPath"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}],"title":"hamiltonianPath()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()","kind":"symbol"}}}